+# Local recording engine implementation plan
+
+> Execute only Task 2 using TDD; parent owns integration.
+
+**Goal:** Nonvisual bounded local recorder, no constructor capture.
+**Architecture:** Immutable explicit source request, safe argument-list ffmpeg launch, async session lifecycle. Separate from existing push-to-talk recorder.
+**Tech:** .NET 8, installed caller-supplied ffmpeg; no new dependencies.
+**Spec:** ../specs/2026-10-28-unified-capabilities-design.md
+
+## API and files
+- RecordingRequest.cs: ScreenRectangle(int X,int Y,int Width,int Height); RecordingRequest(bool Consent, ScreenRectangle? Screen, string? MicrophoneDevice, string? SystemAudioDevice, bool Synthetic, TimeSpan MaxDuration, long MaxBytes).
+- FfmpegRecorder.cs: FfmpegRecorder(string ffmpegPath,string outputRoot); StartAsync(RecordingRequest,CancellationToken) -> Task<RecordingSession>.
+- RecordingSession.cs: Completion Task<RecordingResult>; StopAsync(); CancelAsync(); IAsyncDisposable. Result includes status, exit code, local media path only on success, source request, bounded diagnostic text. Cancellation deletes partial media; crash leaves no published final file. Stop sends q then bounded wait/kill. Duration and output size enforced by ffmpeg and host watchdog.
+- tests/OpenClicky.Recording.Tests: validation, arguments, lifecycle, synthetic encode and ffprobe tests. Evidence in evidence/.
+
+## Constraints and review focus
+No paid/network calls, uploads, hardware tests or UI. Output root must be absolute local fixed-drive directory without reparse ancestors. Generated child names only; no arbitrary output file. No fallback sources. Hardware requires explicit rectangle; audio devices explicitly named DirectShow endpoints. System audio requires an installed exposed loopback endpoint, not arbitrary WASAPI support. Installed ffmpeg reports gdigrab/dshow/lavfi, no WASAPI. No copied code/dependency.
+
+## Steps
+- [ ] Tests first for consent, explicit sources, invalid rectangles/limits, path safety and injection-safe tokenization; observe red.
+- [ ] Implement validation and argument construction; rerun.
+- [ ] Tests first for real synthetic encode/ffprobe, stop, cancellation, crash, byte cap and missing executable.
+- [ ] Implement lifecycle with fragment MP4 recovery-friendly temporary output and bounded diagnostics; rerun focused full recording suite and retain exact exits.
+- [ ] Commit owned paths only; report prerequisites and hardware acceptance gap.
